      "side": 1,
      "message": "I realized that the expected images for identity rescale actions were re-drawing the image at a 1x scale, and then drawing that into the output vs. just drawing the image into the output. For devices like the JioNext (in particular, but other android too), this doubly-impacted its linear filtering precision issues at the boundary of the image.\n\nSkipping the unnecessary draw avoids this, and lets the kAATolerance go back to its original value.",
